@3.1 Loops
.
=3.1 LOOPS
.
=SYNTAX
.
:GP.DO [count]
:    ...
:GP.LOOP
.
=WHAT IT COSTS
.
.  ASM: GP.DO GP.LOOP GP.EXITDO
.    ASM -- a keyword, run by machine code in the GP runtime block. A program
.    using ANY GP keyword pays for the whole block.
.
=DESCRIPTION
.
.Counted loop, modelled on prog8's repeat. A count of 0, or no count, loops
.forever. Loops nest.
.
:GP.EXITDO
.
.Leaves the innermost GP.DO, closing its stack frame. A GOTO out of a GP.DO
.closes its frames too -- see SEC 3.2 -- but GP.EXITDO is two bytes and needs
.no branch target.
.
:GP.DO
:  TICK = TICK + 1
:  IF TICK = 9 THEN GP.EXITDO
:GP.LOOP
.
=EXAMPLE PROGRAM
.
.  LOOPS.EXP.BL -- runnable, in the GPC-BASIC folder
.
=SEE ALSO
.
>18|3.2 Multi-way branch
